On Mon, 12 Nov 2018 18:29:00 -0800
"H. Peter Anvin" <hpa@zytor.com> wrote:

> After a lot of consideration I have decided to not run for re-election to the
> TAB this year. The reason is that I believe that at this particular juncture
> the TAB doesn't need one more white, male, long-term Linux early enthusiast.
> Instead I have come to the conclusion that the professionalization of the
> Linux community that very much need to happen now requires wider representation.
> 
> I am grateful for having been trusted to represent the Linux community in this
> way for the last four years, and I may run again at some point in the future.
> However, this does not feel to me like the right time to do so.
> 
> I would like to urge the community when you cast your ballots to keep this
> need in mind.

Hi Peter,

Sorry to hear that you are not going for re-election. Your input to the
board has been helpful. Thank you for your service.

-- Steve
